why:
Shell cycle 2 (docs/v3/cycles/shell-2.md, P2 shell-2.2): below the `wide` tier, `SplitPage` swaps its panes when `selected` flips, and focus falls to `<body>` both ways. The in-page back link hides the detail that held focus, and an `InnerNav` choice hides the list that held focus (`.evidence/cycle-shell-2/actions.log` B5, `keyboard.log` K8). Seven P3s ride along:
- shell-2.3: Try again on the scaffolded error screen leaves focus on `<body>`;
- shell-2.4: the aside's close returns focus to the first opener row, not the row whose record is open;
- shell-2.5: a palette or More-sheet jump does not hand focus to main;
- shell-2.7: the scaffolded not-found and error screens have no `h1`;
- shell-2.8: the playground's `main.tsx` installs no route screens, so the cycle spreads them per route;
- shell-2.9: a lone enum filter takes three interactions, and its dialog stays open after the choice;
- shell-2.10: the phone `StatGroup` strip stacks four stats in one column.
